    "https://www.brandeis.edu/human-resources/employee-benefits/life-disability-insurance/disability-faculty.html": {
      "title": "Office of Human Resources",
      "description": "Long-Term Disability Insurance for Faculty | Life and Disability Insurance | Employee Benefits | Office of Human Resources | Brandeis University Skip to content Search Search Search this site Search Brandeis.edu Search Menu 2026 Presidential Search Presidential Search Committee and Advisory Council Members Presidential Search Feedback Form Careers at Brandeis Faculty Positions Staff Positions Executive Positions Compensation Massachusetts Pay Transparency Law Annual Benchmarking Process for Staff Employee Benefits Benefits Eligibility End of Benefits Eligibility Time Off and Leaves of Absence 2026 Holiday Schedule Vacation and Sick Time Medical and Family Leave Health Benefits Medical Coverage Understanding Your Medical Coverage Dental Coverage Vision Coverage Other Health Benefits Retirement Savings Plans Retirement Savings Support Retirement Savings Plan Documents Life and Disability Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance for Staff Long-Term Disability Insurance for Faculty Flexible Spending Accounts Limited Purpose FSA Healthcare Flexible Spending Account Dependent Care Flexible Spending Account Health Savings Account (HSA) Tuition Remission Benefits Benefits Changes and Enrollment Employee Discounts and Perks Discount Programs and Special Rates ATMs and Credit Union On-campus Perks Employee Support and Well-Being Employee Assistance Program: KGA Professional Development Salary Planners Talent Advancement Program (TAP) TAP Resources and Training TAP Frequently Asked Questions Training and Professional Development Manager Resources Onboarding Tips for Managers Temporary Staffing Annual Staff Salary Increase Program Frequently Asked Questions Employee Recognition Policies, Forms, and Procedures New Employee Onboarding University Policies and Procedures Background Checks Forms Employment and Income Verification Employee and Labor Relations Resources Disability Accommodation and Complaint Process Fraudulent Unemployment Claims Calendar of Events Meet the Teams Full List of Human Resources Staff Contact Us Home 2026 Presidential Search Presidential Search Committee and Advisory Council Members Presidential Search Feedback Form Careers at Brandeis Faculty Positions Staff Positions Executive Positions Compensation Massachusetts Pay Transparency Law Annual Benchmarking Process for Staff Employee Benefits Benefits Eligibility End of Benefits Eligibility Time Off and Leaves of Absence 2026 Holiday Schedule Vacation and Sick Time Medical and Family Leave Health Benefits Medical Coverage Understanding Your Medical Coverage Dental Coverage Vision Coverage Other Health Benefits Retirement Savings Plans Retirement Savings Support Retirement Savings Plan Documents Life and Disability Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance for Staff Long-Term Disability Insurance for Faculty Flexible Spending Accounts Limited Purpose FSA Healthcare Flexible Spending Account Dependent Care Flexible Spending Account Health Savings Account (HSA) Tuition Remission Benefits Benefits Changes and Enrollment Employee Discounts and Perks Discount Programs and Special Rates ATMs and Credit Union On-campus Perks Employee Support and Well-Being Employee Assistance Program: KGA Professional Development Salary Planners Talent Advancement Program (TAP) TAP Resources and Training TAP Frequently Asked Questions Training and Professional Development Manager Resources Onboarding Tips for Managers Temporary Staffing Annual Staff Salary Increase Program Frequently Asked Questions Employee Recognition Policies, Forms, and Procedures New Employee Onboarding University Policies and Procedures Background Checks Forms Employment and Income Verification Employee and Labor Relations Resources Disability Accommodation and Complaint Process Fraudulent Unemployment Claims Calendar of Events Meet the Teams Full List of Human Resources Staff Contact Us Home Academics Schools Degree Programs Brandeis Online Summer Programs Microcredentials Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Financial Aid Rabb School of Continuing Studies Research Centers and Institutes Funding Resources Athletics Student Life Housing/Community Living Dining Clubs and Organizations Community Service Athletics Arts Rose Art Museum About Our Story Our Jewish Roots Mission and Diversity Statements Fast Facts Visiting Administration Visit Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Giving Popular Resources Campus Calendar Directories Employment Moodle News/Media Orientation Shuttle Schedules Support at Brandeis Workday Sites A-Z Office of Human Resources Home / Employee Benefits / Life and Disability Insurance / Long-Term Disability Insurance for Faculty Long-Term Disability Insurance for Faculty The university provides group long-term total disability insurance to full-time staff (both non-exempt and exempt) and faculty. Summaries of the insurance coverages are listed below. The group long-term disability insurance certificate describes the insurance in detail. The provisions of the formal plan document — not these summaries — shall govern entitlement to benefits, benefit levels and all other matters pertaining to the long-term total disability insurance. Eligibility Regular full-time faculty scheduled to work full time during the academic year (not less than 39 weeks per year) are automatically enrolled on the first day of the month that coincides with or immediately follows the date of employment. The university pays the entire cost of the plan. Definition of Total Disability Total disability under this program is defined as the inability of the employee, by reason of physical disease, injury, pregnancy or mental disorder to perform with reasonable continuity the material duties of his or her own occupation. Benefits Coverage The plan provides the following benefits, which begin on the first day of the month following six consecutive months of total disability and continue during the disability, except as stated under Duration of Benefits. Monthly Income Benefit The monthly income benefit is the amount equal to 60% of the first $25,000 of monthly base salary of predisability earnings, reduced by deductible income, to a $15,000 monthly maximum. This includes any income benefits payable from Social Security, retirement income and workers' compensation (refer to your insurance certificate for more information regarding deductible income). In no event will the disability insurance monthly income benefit be less than $100, even if this amount plus Social Security and workers' compensation benefits brings your total income to more than 60% of salary. Monthly Basic Retirement Plan Contribution Benefit For faculty and senior management group members who are participating in the basic retirement plan and are under age 50, or for those who have attained age 50 but have not yet qualified for the additional 2% university contribution toward the basic retirement plan, the amount of the monthly annuity premium benefit cannot exceed 13% of your eligible predisability earnings. For employees who are age 50 and over and are receiving the additional 2% university contribution toward the basic retirement plan, the monthly annuity premium benefit will be 15% of your eligible predisability earnings. The maximum amount cannot exceed the limits established by the applicable Internal Revenue Code section. Duration of Benefits For those receiving benefits from the university's insurance carrier, disability benefits cease in either or both of the following cases: On the first day of the month in which the period of continuous total disability ends. You fail to provide documentation to the university's insurance carrier, or if earlier, in accordance with the following schedule: Maximum Benefit Period Attained Age Duration of Benefits 61 or younger To age 65, or 3 years, 6 months, if longer 62 3 years, 6 months 63 3 years 64 2 years, 6 months 65 2 years 66 1 year, 9 months 67 1 year, 6 months 68 1 year, 3 months 69 or older 1 year Termination of Group Long-Term Disability Coverage Membership in the group plan terminates if any of the following occurs: You cease to be in a class of eligible faculty. Your work schedule is reduced to part-time status. The group insurance policy terminates. 2026 Presidential Search Careers at Brandeis Compensation Employee Benefits Benefits Eligibility Time Off and Leaves of Absence Health Benefits Retirement Savings Plans Life and Disability Insurance Life Insurance Long-Term Disability Insurance for Staff Long-Term Disability Insurance for Faculty Flexible Spending Accounts Health Savings Account (HSA) Tuition Remission Benefits Benefits Changes and Enrollment Employee Discounts and Perks Employee Support and Well-Being Professional Development Policies, Forms, and Procedures Calendar of Events Meet the Teams Contact Us Home CERTIFICATE AND SUMMARY PLAN DESCRIPTION (pdf) Medical and Family Leave Programs Contact the Benefits Team Email the Human Resources Benefits Team at benefits@brandeis.edu . Find University Policies and Procedures Forms Human Resources Staff Workday at Brandeis Explore Careers at Brandeis Employee Benefits Professional Development Calendar of Events Contact Us Office of Human Resources Bernstein-Marcus, 2nd Floor MS 118 Brandeis University 415 South Street Waltham, MA 02453 781-736-4474 humanresources@brandeis.edu Follow Brandeis Brandeis University ©2026 All rights reserved. University Policies Accessibility Statement Privacy Emergency Services"
