    "https://www.brandeis.edu/audience/fac-staff.html": {
      "title": "Faculty & Staff",
      "description": "Faculty & Staff | Brandeis University Skip to content Search Search Visit Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Giving Popular Resources Campus Calendar Directories Employment Moodle News/Media Orientation Shuttle Schedules Support at Brandeis Workday Sites A-Z Academics Academics Schools School of Arts, Humanities and Culture School of Business and Economics School of Science, Engineering and Technology School of Social Sciences and Social Policy Rabb School of Continuing Studies Degree Programs Brandeis Online Summer Programs Microcredentials Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Financial Aid Rabb School of Continuing Studies Research Research Centers and Institutes Funding Resources Athletics Student Life Student Life Housing/Community Living Dining Clubs and Organizations Community Service Athletics Arts Arts Rose Art Museum About About Our Story Our Jewish Roots Mission and Diversity Statements Fast Facts Overview Schools and Enrollment Faculty Alumni Residence Halls Rankings Athletics Visiting Visiting Brandeis Directions Places to Stay Places to Eat Administration Office of the President Office of the Provost Office of the Executive Vice President, Finance and Administration Leadership Board of Trustees Search Search Academics Academics Academics Schools Degree Programs Brandeis Online Summer Programs Microcredentials Combining academic rigor with career preparation. Brandeis offers rigorous programs through four schools, combining the strengths of a liberal arts education with professional preparation at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Financial Aid Rabb School of Continuing Studies Find your place at Brandeis Explore undergraduate, graduate and continuing education programs at Brandeis University — a private research university on a close-knit campus just outside Boston. Research Research Research Centers and Institutes Funding Resources Explore, collaborate, discover Brandeis research drives discovery and inspires progress. Across disciplines, our faculty and students ask bold questions, push boundaries and pursue knowledge that makes a difference in the world. Athletics Student Life Student Life Student Life Housing/Community Living Dining Clubs and Organizations Community Service Athletics Keep calm and get connected Free pizza at midnight during finals. Clubs that range from a cappella groups to skydiving. If you can’t find your passion here, you can create it — and find other Brandeisians who want to join you. Arts Arts Arts Rose Art Museum Art for everybody's sake Art makes things happen. It bridges cultures and forges understanding. It sparks conversation and inspires creativity. Since our founding, the arts have always played an important role in our commitment to global citizenship and social change. About About About Our Story Our Jewish Roots Mission and Diversity Statements Fast Facts Visiting Administration Learn, engage, lead There is no other place like Brandeis. As a medium-sized private research university with global reach, we are dedicated to first-rate undergraduate education while making groundbreaking discoveries. Our 235-acre campus is located in the suburbs of Boston, a global hub for higher education and innovation. Academics Academics Schools School of Arts, Humanities and Culture School of Business and Economics School of Science, Engineering and Technology School of Social Sciences and Social Policy Rabb School of Continuing Studies Degree Programs Brandeis Online Summer Programs Microcredentials Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Financial Aid Rabb School of Continuing Studies Research Research Centers and Institutes Funding Resources Athletics Student Life Student Life Housing/Community Living Dining Clubs and Organizations Community Service Athletics Arts Arts Rose Art Museum About About Our Story Our Jewish Roots Mission and Diversity Statements Fast Facts Overview Schools and Enrollment Faculty Alumni Residence Halls Rankings Athletics Visiting Visiting Brandeis Directions Places to Stay Places to Eat Administration Office of the President Office of the Provost Office of the Executive Vice President, Finance and Administration Leadership Board of Trustees Visit Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Giving Popular Resources Campus Calendar Directories Employment Moodle News/Media Orientation Shuttle Schedules Support at Brandeis Workday Sites A-Z Faculty & Staff Expand All Academic Resources Academic Calendar Brandeis Library Center for Teaching and Learning Departments and Programs Faculty and Researcher Directory Faculty Handbook Four Schools Moodle (formerly LATTE) Registrar Student Accessibility Support: Information for Faculty Workday Administrative Resources Brandeis Hospitality (Dining) Budget and Planning Business and Finance Brandeis Stationery and Business Card Ordering Portal Campus Planning and Operations Facilities Services Procurement and Business Services Public Safety University Events Governance Board of Trustees Faculty Senate Office of the President Principles of Free Speech and Free Expression Human Resources Benefits Employee Forms Health and Safety Information Holiday Schedule Job Opportunities Paid Time Off Policies and Procedures Support at Brandeis Training and Professional Development Workday News and Information The Brandeis Hoot Brandeis Magazine Brandeis Stories The Justice Campus Calendar Office of Marketing Communications Sexual Misconduct/Title IX Resources Office of Equal Opportunity Prevention, Advocacy & Resource Center Technology Resources Computer Information Help Desk Information Technology Services Managing Your Brandeis Accounts VPN (Virtual Private Network) Zoom Phone Visit Students Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Giving Emergency Information On-campus emergencies: 781-736-3333 Off-campus emergencies: 911 Brandeis Counseling Center: 781-736-3785 Closing and weather emergency hotline: 781-736-2625 Public Safety: 781-736-5000 Sign Up for Emergency Alerts Support at Brandeis Reporting at Brandeis Help Desk Workday Brandeis Directories Brandeis Gmail Headlines from Brandeis Stories Students respond to the Brandeis Plan Brandeis University achieves record-breaking fundraising year Scene at Brandeis: August 2026 New Brandeis Career Network integrates and expands services for undergraduate and graduate students Read more on Brandeis Stories Brandeis Events September 9 Fall Exhibitions Celebration 6 PM September 15 Treats on the ICC: Celebrating Hispanic Heritage Month 10 AM September 15 Get Ready to Connect! Networking Prep 101 4 PM September 17 Brandeis in Business: Industry Networking Night 6 PM View All Events Explore Brandeis The Brandeis Plan to Reinvent the Liberal Arts Brandeis Stories Brandeis Magazine Campus Calendar Make a Gift Applying to Brandeis Undergraduate Admissions Graduate Admissions Rabb School of Continuing Studies Contact Us Brandeis University 415 South Street Waltham, MA 02453 781-736-2000 Contact Us Visiting Brandeis Maps and Directions Register for a Campus Visit Connect With Us Notice of Nondiscrimination : Brandeis University does not discriminate on the basis of race; color; national origin; ethnicity; shared ancestry or ethnic characteristics; caste; sex, pregnancy or related conditions, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, including transgender identity; religion; disability; age; genetics; active military or veteran status; and any other characteristics protected under applicable federal or Massachusetts law in the administration of its educational or employment practices, programs or activities, including admissions. Any concerns or complaints regarding discrimination, harassment or sexual violence should be reported to the Office of Equal Opportunity (OEO). The Director of OEO (781-736-4806; oeo@brandeis.edu ) serves as the Title IX and ADA/Section 504 Coordinator for Brandeis. For more information, please see the Brandeis Policy Against Discrimination, Harassment & Sexual Violence , Formal Complaint Process , and Title IX Grievance Process . Questions about the application of Title IX may be directed to the Director of OEO, the U.S. Department of Education’s Office for Civil Rights , or both. Disability and pregnancy-related accommodations can be requested through Student Accessibility Support (for students) and the Office of Human Resources (for employees). Brandeis University ©2026 All rights reserved. University Policies Privacy Accessibility Statement Emergency Services"
