    "https://www.brandeis.edu/gps/faculty/current-openings/index.html": {
      "title": "Teaching",
      "description": "Teaching at Brandeis Online | Faculty Resources | Brandeis Online | Brandeis University Skip to content Search Search Search Option Search this site Search Brandeis.edu Apply Get Information Information For Current Students Partners Prospective Faculty Prospective Students Search Search Search Option Search this site Search Brandeis.edu Academics Academics Academics Master's Degrees Master's Certificates Academic Resources Take a Course Microcredentials Education Where You Are Offering fully online professional degrees and certificates in today’s most in-demand fields. Admissions & Aid Admissions & Aid Admissions and Aid Apply for Admission Master's Certificate Enrollment International Applicants Military Applicants Tuition and Fees Information Sessions Contact Admissions Begin Your Journey Our flexible rolling admissions process lets you apply and be accepted at any time throughout the year. Student Services Student Services Student Services Advising Campus Resources Career Development Plan for Graduation Networking Opportunities Alumni Course Schedule Course Prerequisites Support Fit to Your Needs We strive to provide a rewarding, flexible and supportive experience for our students. Faculty Resources Faculty Resources Faculty Resources Teaching at Brandeis Online Center for Teaching and Learning Made for Teachers of Tomorrow Our faculty prepare students to succeed in their careers with their unique understanding of the tools, tactics, and trends that define their fields today. Partnerships Partnerships Workforce Development Partnership Education Benefits Everyone Make your employees feel valued and increase their engagement by offering them the opportunity to earn a certificate or a degree. About About About Brandeis Online Why Brandeis Online Staff Contact Us Blog Featured Faculty Outstanding Education, From Anywhere With Brandeis Online, you earn a world-class education at a top, R1 institution from wherever you are. Academics Academics Master's Degrees Master's in Applied Biotechnology and Enterprise Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Applied Data Science and Decision Analytics Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Applied Leadership Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Bioinformatics Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Digital Marketing and Design Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Health Informatics Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Industrial Organizational Psychology and Workforce Analytics Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Information Technology Management Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Jewish Professional Leadership Faculty and Leadership Master's in Project and Program Management Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in Software Engineering Faculty and Advisory Council Master's in User-Centered Design Faculty and Advisory Council Certificate Programs Advanced Therapeutics and Immunology Master's Certificate Agile Project Management Master's Certificate AI-Driven Leadership Master's Certificate Applied Machine Learning & Engineering Master's Certificate Assessment, Selection and Performance Management Master's Certificate Bioinformatics Data Engineering and AI/ML Master's Certificate Biotechnology Leadership and Entrepreneurship Master's Certificate Change Management Master's Certificate Cheminformatics Master’s Certificate Clinical Data Science and Analytics Master's Certificate Computational Biology for Computer Scientists Master's Certificate Content Marketing Master's Certificate Cybersecurity Master's Certificate Data Engineering, Automation and Cybersecurity Governance Master's Certificate Data Engineering and Cloud Analytics Master's Certificate Digital Accessibility Master's Certificate Digital Health Project Management and Implementation Master's Certificate Digital Marketing Master's Certificate Drug Discovery Informatics Master's Certificate Enterprise Cloud Technologies and Intelligent Systems Operations Master's Certificate Genomics Master's Certificate Healthcare Analytics Master's Certificate Faculty Jewish Professional Leadership Master's Certificate Marketing Analytics Master's Certificate Project Management Master's Certificate Software Architecture Master's Certificate Software Development Master's Certificate Software Engineering with Artificial Intelligence Master's Certificate Sustainable Biotechnology Manufacturing and Compliance Master's Certificate Talent Analytics and Strategic Workforce Planning Master's Certificate UX Research Master's Certificate Academic Resources Take a Course Microcredentials AI Fundamentals for STEM Professionals Communicating Complex Ideas with Clarity Driving Innovation: Skills for ROI Industry-Focused Prompt Engineering for ROI-Driven Results FAQ Student Services Student Services Advising Campus Resources Career Development Plan for Graduation Networking Opportunities Alumni Course Schedule Course Prerequisites Faculty Resources Faculty Resources Teaching at Brandeis Online Incoming Faculty Resources (Login Required) Center for Teaching and Learning Partnerships Workforce Development Partnership About About Brandeis Online Why Brandeis Online Staff Contact Us Blog Featured Faculty Information For Current Students Partners Prospective Faculty Prospective Students Apply Get Information Brandeis Online Teaching at Brandeis Online Home / Faculty Resources / Teaching at Brandeis Online Brandeis Online adjunct faculty are active industry leaders in their field. Their professional expertise is brought to the classroom via online class discussions, projects and lectures. Instructors are part-time and work fully online, with no requirement to appear on campus. Contact us to learn more. Brandeis University is a medium-sized private research university with a global reach, dedicated to first-rate education and the making of groundbreaking discoveries, and is consistently ranked among the nation's top universities. The Rabb School of Continuing Studies emerged in 1992 to support the university in its mission of academic excellence and access by embracing continuous lifelong learning and development, regardless of a student's age, as well as the unconventional and creative values held by the institution. Over the years the University has continuously invested in online programming and expanded Brandeis Online across schools. All Brandeis Online programs are developed using the best practices in online learning. Courses are 8-10-weeks long and follow a 100% asynchronous teaching model in the online learning environment, with no set days or times for interaction. Current Faculty Openings As our programs continue to expand to meet the demands of jobseekers and lifelong learners today, we are always recruiting expert faculty. If you do not see a position that aligns with your experience, please feel free to still apply to a program — we will keep your application on file for review when a potential matching position arises. EXPLORE FACULTY OPENINGS Teaching Standards Faculty who teach with Brandeis Online are expected to adhere to the following teaching standards. Faculty will receive feedback regarding their adherence to these standards approximately four weeks after the session ends. EXPLORE TEACHING STANDARDS How to Apply Brandeis Online welcomes applications for its adjunct faculty pool on an ongoing basis. The application process consists of the online application (including an uploaded current resume or CV) and, if subject matter qualifications are met, a series of interviews at the discretion of the Program Chair and Director of Program Development. General Qualifications for Adjunct Faculty Brandeis Online faculty have earned (at the minimum) a master's degree, with many holding terminal academic degrees and industry-specific credentials. Previous experience teaching online is not required, as Brandeis Online offers a comprehensive training program for qualified faculty. Below are the general qualifications to teach: Active professional employment in an industry closely aligned to the field of study Master's degree or higher aligned to the field of study Strong communication skills when conveying complex information and promoting in-depth engagement on course topics Strong interpersonal skills when relating to students The ability to devote adequate time to courses, including responding to students and providing meaningful feedback in a timely manner Teaching experience preferred; online teaching or learning experience preferred Job opportunities for the Brandeis Online community We also invite both job seekers and recruiters to follow the Brandeis Online LinkedIn page , where you can connect with other members of our community, hear about upcoming events and webinars, and keep track of new initiatives. Brandeis University is an equal opportunity employer which does not discriminate against any applicant or employee on the basis of race, color, ancestry, religious creed, gender identity and expression, national or ethnic origin, sex, sexual orientation, pregnancy, age, genetic information, disability, caste, military or veteran status or any other category protected by law (also known as membership in a \"protected class\"). Faculty Resources Teaching at Brandeis Online Incoming Faculty Resources (Login Required) Center for Teaching and Learning Brandeis Online 415 South Street Waltham, MA 02453 781-736-8787 online@brandeis.edu Back to Brandeis.edu Apply to Brandeis Online First Time Applicants International Applicants Alumni Applicants Take the Next Step Explore Master's Degrees and Certificates Connect with Our Team Meet Our Students Financial Options Partner with Brandeis Online ©2026 Brandeis University Privacy Policy Accessibility"
